                <invention-title lang="de">ÖLZIRKULATIONSSYSTEM FÜR HYBRIDE ELEKTRISCHE MOTOREN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SYSTÈME DE CIRCULATION D'HUILE POUR MOTEUR ÉLECTRIQUE HYBRIDE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">OIL CIRCULATION SYSTEM FOR HYBRID ELECTRIC ENGINE</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A hybrid electric propulsion system including: a gas turbine engine comprising a low speed spool (30), a high speed spool (32), and a combustor; a lubrication circuit (290) comprising a bearing compartment (296), a supply pump (292), and a scavenger pump (298); an electric motor (282) configured to augment rotational power of the low speed spool (30) or the high speed spool (32); and a controller (256) operable to: control the electric motor (282) based upon a pressure differential between an interior of the bearing compartment (296) and an exterior of the bearing compartment (296) and to drive rotation of the low speed spool (30) and/or the high speed spool (32) via the electric motor (282) responsive to a thrust command while fuel flow to the combustor is inhibited.</p>
            </abstract>
